    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 2  Bribing a foreign public official",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) provides a benefit to another person; or\n(ii) causes a benefit to be provided to another person; or\n(iii) offers to provide, or promises to provide, a benefit to\nanother person; or\n(iv) causes an offer of the provision of a benefit, or a\npromise of the provision of a benefit, to be made to\nanother person; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does so with the intention of\nimproperly influencing a foreign public official (who may be\nthe other person) in order to obtain or retain business or a\nbusiness or personal advantage (whether or not for the\nfirst-mentioned person).\nNote:\nSee also section 70.2A. For defences, see sections 70.3 and 70.4.\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):\n(a) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to\ninfluence a particular foreign public official; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to obtain\nor retain particular business or a particular business or\npersonal advantage; and\n(c) business, or a business or personal advantage, does not need\nto be actually obtained or retained.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) provides a benefit to another person; or\n(ii) causes a benefit to be provided to another person; or\n(iii) offers to provide, or promises to provide, a benefit to\nanother person; or\n(iv) causes an offer of the provision of a benefit, or a\npromise of the provision of a benefit, to be made to\nanother person; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does so with the intention of\nimproperly influencing a foreign public official (who may be\nthe other person) in order to obtain or retain business or a\nbusiness or personal advantage (whether or not for the\nfirst-mentioned person).\nNote:\nSee also section 70.2A. For defences, see sections 70.3 and 70.4.\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):\n(a) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to\ninfluence a particular foreign public official; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to obtain\nor retain particular business or a particular business or\npersonal advantage; and\n(c) business, or a business or personal advantage, does not need\nto be actually obtained or retained.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27cb55da9b2a0444f4cf602cb0856660e4c6398fa8c8dfb11965933f40ce32d7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 2  Bribing a foreign public official",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) provides a benefit to another person; or\n(ii) causes a benefit to be provided to another person; or\n(iii) offers to provide, or promises to provide, a benefit to\nanother person; or\n(iv) causes an offer of the provision of a benefit, or a\npromise of the provision of a benefit, to be made to\nanother person; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does so with the intention of\nimproperly influencing a foreign public official (who may be\nthe other person) in order to obtain or retain business or a\nbusiness or personal advantage (whether or not for the\nfirst-mentioned person).\nNote:\nSee also section 70.2A. For defences, see sections 70.3 and 70.4.\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):\n(a) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to\ninfluence a particular foreign public official; and\n(b) the first-mentioned person does not need to intend to obtain\nor retain particular business or a particular business or\npersonal advantage; and\n(c) business, or a business or personal advantage, does not need\nto be actually obtained or retained.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
