    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70(3) 2A  Improper influence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether influence is improper for the purposes of\nparagraph 70.2(1)(b), a trier of fact may have regard to the\nfollowing:\n(a) the recipient or intended recipient of the benefit;\n(b) the nature of the benefit;\n(c) the manner of the provision of the benefit (or, if applicable,\nthe offered or promised manner of the provision of the\nbenefit);\n(d) whether the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the\nvalue of any consideration provided or purported to have\nbeen provided for the benefit;\n(e) if the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to provide\nthe benefit was made, in the absence of any legal obligation\nto do so—that fact;\n(f) whether the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit was made, dishonestly;\n(g) whether, and to what extent, the provision of the benefit, or\nthe offer or promise to provide the benefit, is recorded or\ndocumented;\n(h) if the provision of the benefit, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit, is recorded or documented:\n(i) the accuracy of the record or documentation; and\n(ii) whether the record or documentation is consistent with\nthe ordinary practices of the person who made the\nrecord or documentation;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining whether influence is improper for the purposes of\nparagraph 70.2(1)(b), a trier of fact may have regard to the\nfollowing:\n(a) the recipient or intended recipient of the benefit;\n(b) the nature of the benefit;\n(c) the manner of the provision of the benefit (or, if applicable,\nthe offered or promised manner of the provision of the\nbenefit);\n(d) whether the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the\nvalue of any consideration provided or purported to have\nbeen provided for the benefit;\n(e) if the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to provide\nthe benefit was made, in the absence of any legal obligation\nto do so—that fact;\n(f) whether the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit was made, dishonestly;\n(g) whether, and to what extent, the provision of the benefit, or\nthe offer or promise to provide the benefit, is recorded or\ndocumented;\n(h) if the provision of the benefit, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit, is recorded or documented:\n(i) the accuracy of the record or documentation; and\n(ii) whether the record or documentation is consistent with\nthe ordinary practices of the person who made the\nrecord or documentation;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-ltl-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "302915aaf5c182071f7a3518b016ff511ed662abd188f96da683f3c1989a74e6",
      "skos:note": "Influence is improper if the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the consideration provided."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70(3) 2A  Improper influence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether influence is improper for the purposes of\nparagraph 70.2(1)(b), a trier of fact may have regard to the\nfollowing:\n(a) the recipient or intended recipient of the benefit;\n(b) the nature of the benefit;\n(c) the manner of the provision of the benefit (or, if applicable,\nthe offered or promised manner of the provision of the\nbenefit);\n(d) whether the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the\nvalue of any consideration provided or purported to have\nbeen provided for the benefit;\n(e) if the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to provide\nthe benefit was made, in the absence of any legal obligation\nto do so—that fact;\n(f) whether the benefit was provided, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit was made, dishonestly;\n(g) whether, and to what extent, the provision of the benefit, or\nthe offer or promise to provide the benefit, is recorded or\ndocumented;\n(h) if the provision of the benefit, or the offer or promise to\nprovide the benefit, is recorded or documented:\n(i) the accuracy of the record or documentation; and\n(ii) whether the record or documentation is consistent with\nthe ordinary practices of the person who made the\nrecord or documentation;\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-norm",
