      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) In determining whether influence is improper for the purposes of paragraph 70.2(1)(b), a trier of fact may have regard to..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Improper influence is prohibited if the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the consideration provided.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the recipient or intended recipient of the benefit;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The provision of the benefit, or the offer or promise to provide the benefit, occurs before the consideration is provided.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the manner of the provision of the benefit (or, if applicable, the offered or promised manner of the provision of the benefit);"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-3-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The consideration is provided before the influence is improper.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) whether the value of the benefit is disproportionate to the value of any consideration provided or purported to have been provided for the benefit;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 After subsection 70.3(2) of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(2A) A person does not commit an offence against section 70.2 if:\n(a) the person’s conduct occurred in relation to a foreign public\nofficial (the relevant foreign public official); and\n(b) the relevant foreign public official is covered by\nparagraph (m) of the definition of foreign public official in\nsection 70.1 because the relevant foreign public official is a\ncandidate to be a particular foreign public official (the\nsubstantive foreign public official); and\n(c) assuming that the first-mentioned person’s conduct had\noccurred wholly in the place, the foreign country or the part\nof the foreign country, as the case may be, (the relevant\nplace) referred to in the item of the table in subsection (1)\nthat would be applicable if the first-mentioned person’s\nconduct had occurred in relation to the substantive foreign\npublic official, a written law in force in the relevant place\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\nNo. 5, 2024\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Combatting Foreign Bribery) Act\npermits the provision of the benefit to the relevant foreign\npublic official.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2A). See subsection 13.3(3).",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n(2A) A person does not commit an offence against section 70.2 if:\n(a) the person’s conduct occurred in relation to a foreign public\nofficial (the relevant foreign public official); and\n(b) the relevant foreign public official is covered by\nparagraph (m) of the definition of foreign public official in\nsection 70.1 because the relevant foreign public official is a\ncandidate to be a particular foreign public official (the\nsubstantive foreign public official); and\n(c) assuming that the first-mentioned person’s conduct had\noccurred wholly in the place, the foreign country or the part\nof the foreign country, as the case may be, (the relevant\nplace) referred to in the item of the table in subsection (1)\nthat would be applicable if the first-mentioned person’s\nconduct had occurred in relation to the substantive foreign\npublic official, a written law in force in the relevant place\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\nNo. 5, 2024\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Combatting Foreign Bribery) Act\npermits the provision of the benefit to the relevant foreign\npublic official.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2A). See subsection 13.3(3).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-7-norm"
        },
