    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70 5C  Meaning of annual turnover",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, the annual turnover of a body\ncorporate, during the turnover period, is the sum of the values of all\nthe supplies that the body corporate, and any body corporate\nrelated to the body corporate, have made, or are likely to make,\nduring that period, other than the following supplies:\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate;\n(b) supplies that are input taxed;\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999);\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on.\n(2) Expressions used in this section that are also used in the A New Tax\nSystem (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same meaning\nin this section as they have in that Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, the annual turnover of a body\ncorporate, during the turnover period, is the sum of the values of all\nthe supplies that the body corporate, and any body corporate\nrelated to the body corporate, have made, or are likely to make,\nduring that period, other than the following supplies:\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate;\n(b) supplies that are input taxed;\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999);\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on.\n(2) Expressions used in this section that are also used in the A New Tax\nSystem (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same meaning\nin this section as they have in that Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e793f1cb0730555efba3dad5bde45e5435e8ae421af7521024760e9dc93129c8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70 5C  Meaning of annual turnover",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, the annual turnover of a body\ncorporate, during the turnover period, is the sum of the values of all\nthe supplies that the body corporate, and any body corporate\nrelated to the body corporate, have made, or are likely to make,\nduring that period, other than the following supplies:\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate;\n(b) supplies that are input taxed;\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999);\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on.\n(2) Expressions used in this section that are also used in the A New Tax\nSystem (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same meaning\nin this section as they have in that Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-5-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70(1) 5C  Meaning of annual turnover",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024#sch-1-sec-70-5-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, the annual turnover of a body\ncorporate, during the turnover period, is the sum of the values of all\nthe supplies that the body corporate, and any body corporate\nrelated to the body corporate, have made, or are likely to make,\nduring that period, other than the following supplies:\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate;\n(b) supplies that are input taxed;\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999);\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, the annual turnover of a body\ncorporate, during the turnover period, is the sum of the values of all\nthe supplies that the body corporate, and any body corporate\nrelated to the body corporate, have made, or are likely to make,\nduring that period, other than the following supplies:\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate;\n(b) supplies that are input taxed;\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999);\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-combatting-foreign-bribery-act-2024-sch-1-sec-70-5"
      },
